CHAP{Key-word : "Austenite"}
PART{Thermomechanical characteristics (Vincent, 2002) [5]}


    Output data in table TAB1 :
    ---------------------------

    - Mechanical properties :

    TAB1 . 'YOUN' : EVOLUTION type object, Young's modulus (Pa)
                    according to temperature (degC)

    TAB1 . 'NU'   : FLOTTANT type object, Poisson's ratio

    TAB1 . 'TALP  : FLOTTANT type object, reference temperature for the
                    thermal expansion (degC)

    TAB1 . 'ALPH' : EVOLUTION type object, thermal expansion
                    according to temperature (degC)

    TAB1 . 'DCOM' : FLOTTANT type object, difference in compactness between
                    austenite and ferrite (austenite more compact).
                    Thermal expansion-like quantity.

    TAB1 . 'SIGY' : EVOLUTION type object, yield stress (Pa)
                    according to temperature (degC)

    TAB1 . 'ECRO' : NUAGE type object, hardening curves (Sig. Vs. Eps.Plas.)
                    (Pa) Vs. temperature (degC).


